# MEASUREMENT fragment: drop subsystems this board has no hardware or user for.
#
#   KERNEL_CONFIG=slim build/build.sh kernel
#     -> build/out/h713-kernel-slim.fit
#
# Not a shipping change on its own -- build it, compare Image/Image.gz against
# the production build, and fold into hy200_qz713df_a1_defconfig only if the
# delta is worth the review. The point of a separate fragment is that the
# comparison is measurable rather than argued.
#
# Sizes below are built-in.a text+data, i.e. an UPPER BOUND on what the Image
# loses: they include .init sections freed after boot and sections the linker
# may garbage-collect.
#
#   ATA        ~210 KiB  libata core. There is not a single sata/ahci node in
#                        sun50i-h713.dtsi, and CONFIG_SATA_AHCI is not even
#                        set, so this is the core with no driver behind it.
#                        NOTE this does NOT touch SCSI: USB_STORAGE=y and
#                        BLK_DEV_SD=y are both on, a projector reading a USB
#                        stick is a real use case, and USB storage needs SCSI.
#   CAN         ~46 KiB  CAN bus. No controller on this SoC.
#   NFS_FS     ~254 KiB  NFS client, and it drags SUNRPC with it (NFSD is not
#                        set, so nothing else holds SUNRPC up). The rootfs is
#                        ext4 on eMMC; ROOT_NFS and NFS_V4 go too.
#   IO_URING   ~166 KiB  NOT DISABLED HERE, and it cannot be without a bigger
#                        decision: init/Kconfig declares it
#                        `bool "Enable IO uring support" if EXPERT` with
#                        `default y`, so with CONFIG_EXPERT unset the prompt is
#                        hidden and olddefconfig puts it straight back. Turning
#                        it off means CONFIG_EXPERT=y, which unhides a large
#                        number of other symbols and changes defaults well
#                        beyond this one. Worth 166 KiB, but not silently.
#                        (The build guard caught this rather than shipping a
#                        fragment that quietly did nothing.)
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT TOUCHED, because these are product decisions rather than
# dead weight, and someone should make them on purpose:
#
#   SOUND/SND  ~413 KiB  Audio bring-up has not happened yet, but a projector
#                        wants audio. Removing it now just means adding it back.
#   IPV6       ~415 KiB  Arguably unnecessary on an appliance, but Debian
#                        userspace assumes it in places and the failure mode is
#                        confusing rather than obvious.
#   BT         ~625 KiB  Bluetooth works and is part of the product.
#   mac80211 + wireless  Required for WiFi.
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION=""
# CONFIG_ATA is not set
# CONFIG_CAN is not set
# CONFIG_NFS_FS is not set
